    {
      "id": "term-eng-t41",
      "termNumber": "41",
      "engSourceId": "eng-t41-v1",
      "title": "donkey",
      "sourceFile": "eng/json/004.content.json",
      "selectedBy": "passage",
      "text": {
        "status": "source",
        "sourceId": "eng-t41-v1",
        "html": "<p>A <b>donkey</b> is an animal that is big enough to carry heavy loads or people. People kept donkeys to help them work in their fields or to carry burdens. A donkey was considered an animal of peace, in contrast to a horse, which is a larger animal that soldiers rode on when they were fighting battles in war.</p>",
