    {
      "id": "term-eng-t88",
      "termNumber": "88",
      "engSourceId": "eng-t88-v1",
      "title": "Lord",
      "sourceFile": "eng/json/012.content.json",
      "selectedBy": "passage",
      "text": {
        "status": "source",
        "sourceId": "eng-t88-v1",
        "html": "<p>In some cases in the New Testament, <b>Lord</b> refers to God himself. It is the way the <data class=\"resource-ref\" data-content-id=\"eng-t77-v2\" data-resource-code=\"FIAKeyTerms\">Jewish</data> people referred to God when they did not want to say his name because they respected him so much.</p>",
        "textSha256": "c7993b3f88016ee3881f444438f372efbf7dbd5677ba0f9e2b613ef67bc9d7f2",
